  - kind: 1
    value: |-
      ## 14. Map with MapLibre

      [`demo1_zet_map.html`](demo1_zet_map.html) shows the three tile endpoints from section 11 on a map with [MapLibre GL JS](https://maplibre.org/maplibre-gl-js/docs/), styled like the hook slides:

      | Layer | Endpoint | Source layer | Style |
      |---|---|---|---|
      | Tram 6 track | `/zet/vt/tram-lines/{z}/{x}/{y}` | `tram_lines` | Light blue line (`#80B3C5`) |
      | Stops A–D | `/zet/vt/tram-stations/{z}/{x}/{y}` | `tram_stations` | White circle with the `tram-station` icon (`media/large/tram-station.png`), the stop code, and the stop name from zoom 15 |
      | Trams | `/zet/vt/vehicles/{z}/{x}/{y}` | `vehicles` | Teal circle (`#00688C`) with a white outline: positions of the last 2 minutes, older ones fade (`AGE_S`), reloaded every 10 seconds |

      The basemap is the dark style of [OpenFreeMap](https://openfreemap.org/) (OpenStreetMap data, no API key), recoloured to the Redwood dark palette. Oracle's own `osm-dark-matter` style has the same layout, but its tiles need an Oracle Maps token.

      **Show the map:**
      1. In the `10_HrOUG` folder, start a local web server. The page loads the stop icon from `../media`, which browsers block for pages opened directly from disk. `--bind 127.0.0.1` keeps the server, and the files in the folder, private to your machine:
         ```bash
         python -m http.server 8000 --bind 127.0.0.1
         ```
      2. Open `http://localhost:8000/scripts/demo1_zet_map.html?ords=https://<adb-host>/ords/<schema>`. Instead of `?ords=`, you can set `DEFAULT_ORDS_BASE` in the file. `&refresh=5` reloads the trams every 5 seconds instead of 10.
      3. Check the status line at the bottom of the panel:
         * **"N trams with positions in the last 2 minutes"**: the map is live.
         * **"No tram positions in the last 2 minutes"**: the tiles work, but no new positions arrived. The tram layer shows live data only, so the loader job from section 13 must be running. The July data from section 7.2 is older than 2 minutes and doesn't appear; replaying it needs an "as of" time for `ZET_TILES.VEHICLES`.
         * **"Tile request to ORDS failed"**: check the URL and open the browser console. If it reports a CORS error, allow the page's origin for the tile module:
           ```sql
           BEGIN
             ORDS.SET_MODULE_ORIGINS_ALLOWED(
               p_module_name     => 'zet.tiles',
               p_origins_allowed => 'http://localhost:8000');
             COMMIT;
           END;
           /
           ```
      4. Click a tram or a stop for details. The URL hash (`#zoom/lat/lon`) keeps the current view, so a reload or a bookmark returns to it.

      To test one tile without the map (stop A, zoom 14):

      ```bash
      curl -s -o tile.pbf -w "%{http_code} %{content_type} %{size_download} bytes\n" https://<adb-host>/ords/<schema>/zet/vt/tram-stations/14/8919/5841
      ```

      References:
      * [ORDS.SET_MODULE_ORIGINS_ALLOWED](https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/oracle/oracle-rest-data-services/25.4/orddg/ORDS-reference.html)
      * [MapLibre GL JS: vector sources](https://maplibre.org/maplibre-style-spec/sources/#vector)
      * [OpenFreeMap](https://openfreemap.org/)
    languageId: markdown
